{%- comment -%}
  Senseless — header/footer brand touches
  Superseded for the header by the fully custom `senseless-header` section (Strand 2), which now
  owns all header styling/behaviour. The previous "Find your strength" nav pill + Horizon
  `.header-menu` hover overrides were removed with that rebuild (the pill no longer belongs in the
  header). The footer still uses Horizon's native footer and needs no overrides here.
  Now also home to the brand mapping for two Shopify-owned components we don't fork:
  the <shopify-account> customer-account component and the Horizon cart drawer. We set their
  CSS custom properties here (head, loads AFTER the bundled theme CSS) instead of editing the
  vendor snippet, mapping each to existing Senseless tokens (no new hex).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- style -%}
  /* ── Customer account component (<shopify-account>) ──────────────────────────────
     header-actions.liquid (vendor) already maps the component's PRIMARY variables to theme
     tokens: --color-accent → #6B3FA0, --color-accent-text → on-accent, --color-background,
     --color-text, fonts (Montserrat) and radii. The component DERIVES the rest of its surface
     (signed-in avatar, accent-hover, border, shadow, subdued/card/control tones) from those
     primaries, so the opened account sheet is already brand-coherent — and those derived
     variables can't be overridden from the page without !important (the component re-declares
     them). We therefore pin only the signed-in avatar to brand (the one the brief calls out),
     so it's brand-locked rather than relying on the derivation. Signed-out avatar is already
     slot-replaced with the site account icon in header-actions. */
  shopify-account {
    --shopify-account-signed-in-avatar-color-background: var(--brand-primary) !important;
    --shopify-account-signed-in-avatar-color-text: var(--color-primary-button-text, var(--bg-surface)) !important;
    --shopify-account-signed-in-avatar-size: 28px !important; /* matches the header icon footprint / fallback avatar */
    --shopify-account-avatar-size: 28px !important;
  }

  /* ── Cart drawer ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Horizon's drawer already inherits Senseless tokens (canvas #f7f7f5 surface, Montserrat,
     #6B3FA0 primary checkout button via the shared .button styles, 14px button radius). Pin the
     heading to brand ink (was scheme foreground at 81% black) so it matches PDP/site headings.
     Behaviour unchanged — auto-open stays OFF (count-only on add). */
  .cart-drawer__dialog .cart-drawer__heading {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  /* ── Judge.me stars → Senseless starburst (EXPERIMENT) ──────────────────────────────
     Replaces Judge.me's star glyph with the brand starburst via mask-image. Filled = brand
     purple, empty = light purple-grey, half = 50/50 split. Works whether Judge.me renders
     stars as an icon-font or inline SVG (hide the glyph with transparent colour, paint the
     element's box through the starburst mask). Revert = delete this block.
     If it looks wrong, fall back to the plain #6B3FA0 recolour in Judge.me settings. */
  .jdgm-star.jdgm--on,
  .jdgm-star.jdgm--off,
  .jdgm-star.jdgm--half {
    color: transparent !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent !important;  /* kill residual glyph (the | artifact) */
    text-shadow: none !important;
    -webkit-mask: url("{{ 'senseless-asterisk.svg' | asset_url }}") center / contain no-repeat;
            mask: url("{{ 'senseless-asterisk.svg' | asset_url }}") center / contain no-repeat;
    background-color: var(--brand-primary) !important;
  }
  .jdgm-star.jdgm--off {
    background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-primary) 20%, var(--bg-surface, #fff)) !important;
  }
  .jdgm-star.jdgm--half {
    background-color: transparent !important;
    background-image: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--brand-primary) 0 50%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-primary) 20%, var(--bg-surface, #fff)) 50% 100%) !important;
  }
{%- endstyle -%}
